{"id": "EUVD-2026-95816", "enisaUuid": "d3999ab8-08cf-3700-b5e3-b71c2e10c878", "description": "Use-after-free vulnerability in VFS in Google gVisor prior to release 20260831.0 on all platforms allows a local attacker with standard container privileges to achieve code execution in the host sentry process by double-freeing the backing MemoryFile from an in-sandbox overlay filesystem. The sentry process remains confined by host-level Linux seccomp and namespace boundaries.", "datePublished": "2026-10-09T14:44:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T18:15:18", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/google/gvisor/commit/90bc4fc36fe442257a06ba15df00371561c183ed", "https://github.com/google/gvisor/commit/25c75149bc0eeaa6a3a49b9bbe3473588b2af6df", "https://github.com/google/gvisor/commit/e4efb89c787ef15b09e68d561f1303380e1d5a77"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-95702", "GHSA-hv4v-f9v2-r8c2"], "assigner": "Google", "epss": 0.08, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b4bb8f5b-421a-3c1d-9f1a-522c55fbc1c8", "product": {"name": "Gvisor", "vendor": {"name": "Google"}}, "product_version": "0 <20260831.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "998a91f2-c2a7-3dae-b879-5ccae8e0fae3", "vendor": {"name": "Google"}}], "isExploited": false}